  "notes": "Owner-authorized step 7 substantive re-review (Ruling 40 step 7; rulings of 2026-10-08 and 2026-10-09), read against the ratified theorem text and the code, tests, probes and proofs at HEAD 78c938b6. Review record: work/security-audit-2026-09-22-r12/STEP7-R2-REVIEW-4.md (CONFIRMED). This record binds the claim, its premise texts, its logical dependency claims, and the semantic components of its supporting units (review_digest); not toolchain, Bazel or policy identity. Re-read at HEAD 4f9eb062 after the CodeQL remediation (work/security-audit-2026-09-22-r12/CODEQL-REREVIEW.md): test sources only; the accept-any-server TLS test verifier was replaced by verification against the test's server CA, no test or assertion removed or weakened. Claim, premises, dependencies and entry text unchanged. Re-read at the nonce-literal cleanup (work/security-audit-2026-09-22-r12/NONCE-REREVIEW.md): hard-coded request nonces in tests whose property does not depend on the nonce's value now come from the test-only `unique_test_nonce`, dev-dependency wiring and one helper in mcp-re-test-paths added; every deterministic vector, committed fixture, collision-shaped input and malformed-nonce control keeps its literal; no test or assertion removed or weakened. Claim, premises, dependencies and entry text unchanged. Re-read after CI formatting (rustfmt over the nonce-cleanup test edits) and the clock-free unique_test_nonce (process id, process address, counter; work/security-audit-2026-09-22-r12/NONCE-REREVIEW.md): formatting and the test-only helper only; claim, premises, dependencies and entry text unchanged. Re-read after the replay-race salt stopped defaulting a missing clock to a literal 0 (work/security-audit-2026-09-22-r12/NONCE-REREVIEW.md): one test helper only; claim, premises, dependencies and entry text unchanged. Re-read in the post-architecture assurance-closure campaign (MCPRE-218, #1171) against the semantic changes to its supporting units over a0b944c4..72127a07, recorded in verification/reviews/packets/assurance-closure-rereview-2026-10-14.md, and ratified in the owner's batch ruling of 2026-10-14 (verification/reviews/rulings/mcpre-218-assurance-closure-2026-10-14.md). Its own claim is unchanged. Its fingerprint moved only through the dependency claim of THM-0092, corrected under the same ruling; re-read against the corrected THM-0092 text, which states the same promise, and the composition holds. Agent re-review for epic #1201 (ADR-MCPRE-070), prepared under the owner's directive of 2026-10-21 transcribed in verification/reviews/rulings/epic-1201-authority-closure-2026-10-21.md. This record is NOT an owner signature: it attests the agent's substantive reading only, and the owner's ratification is the ledger line that ruling file names, which does not exist when this record is written. Read in verification/reviews/packets/epic-1201-assurance-closure-2026-10-21.md: verdict CLEAN-NOTE, cause dependency change (THM-0101) + implementation change.  Re-read after the owner directions of 2026-10-21 were applied (packet section 'Addendum 2'): THM-0135 joins its dependency closure (direction 4). Its statement, consequence and scope are unchanged; under the required audit posture the committed execution intent is a pre-dispatch obligation the validated deployment selected, established by its owner before the backend is reached, which is this root's shape. Its test_sources also moved through the added O5 test. Evidence class as registered; V0 units are tested and probed, not machine-checked proofs.",
